+From 329e66df37adc7f71ac25215dad9ddec835fdc1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:42:15 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: Dolby Vision CM v4.0 metadata and L2
+ trims
+
+The engine can add neutral CM v4.0 blocks (L3, L9, L11 and L254) to
+the metadata of a CM v2.9 stream and leave its L2 trims out, as the
+libreelec-x86-DV build does (CB1's cb1_cmv40). Add the settings for
+it to the Dolby Vision group of Player / Videos and of the video
+settings: Add CM v4.0 metadata (Off, Without L2 trims only, Always,
+Auto, Auto 2), Auto's trigger, Auto 2's headroom, the TV peak
+luminance those rules go by, and Remove L2 trims.
+
+They apply from the next picture, without reopening the engine's
+stream. Player information shows what was sent where they ask for
+anything.
+
+Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
